    "blogtextliquid_LBJgtB": {
      "type": "editorial--blog-text-liquid",
      "custom_css": [],
      "name": "Blog Text Liquid",
      "settings": {
        "text_content": "<p>There is a lot of fragrance advice floating around out there, and an alarming amount of it is completely wrong. Passed down through department store counters, social media videos, and magazine columns, these myths cause shoppers to waste money on overpriced bottles and apply their perfume in ways that ruin its performance.</p><p>In reality, perfumery is an exact science of molecular volatility, evaporation rates, and organic chemistry. Let's separate fact from fiction and leave the six most stubborn perfume myths behind for good.</p>"
      }
    },
